 {'id':'C3','proposal':'Replace the prime-power order proof split by the complete divisibility spectrum p^(k+1) | g^m-1 iff p^k | m.','decision':'retain_narrow','nearest_prior':['E099/E108 Pell power approximation budgets (different subject)'],'delta':'No LTE, p-adic valuation spectrum, exact prime-power order or arbitrary-exponent spectrum proposal was found in the 28 packet manuscripts and targeted supporting-code searches.','limits':'Preserve m=0,k=0 and exact first-lift hypotheses; give the full mathematical proof and avoid circular dependence on the order theorem being shortened.'},
 {'id':'C4','proposal':'Remove sixteen_pow_bound induction by setting t=4^r, rewriting 16^r=t^2, and proving 4t+2<=t^2 for t>=16.','decision':'retain_narrow','nearest_prior':['E151 fixed-index-six Pell anchor','E143 geometric-sum induction reuse'],'delta':'This is a concrete exponential-to-polynomial reduction at NativePellPower.sixteen_pow_bound, absent from the prior claims; it does not re-propose Pell approximation or geometric-sum libraries.','limits':'Count the normal-form identities and proof of t>=16; do not infer compiler speed from source length.'},
