 {'id':'C6','proposal':'Use the actual periodic top-field reset to normalize each cell by an acyclic finite fold from zero and prove locality under edits.','decision':'retain_narrow','nearest_prior':['E031 scalar reset facts','E066 explicit least/greatest full-cycle carry formulas','E073 carry uniqueness with fixed raw and digits','E154 signed-prefix concatenation direction'],'delta':'A proved synchronization/reset boundary splits the cyclic normalizer into independent cells. This gives a constructive per-cell evaluation and edit-locality theorem, beyond closed formulas or uniqueness of a full cycle.','limits':'Do not replace the general arbitrary-predecessor fixedpoint theorem. Derive every cell reset from the actual raw budget and cover N=1/wraparound; raw convolution changes can affect neighboring cells, so locality must name the raw cells that stay equal.'},
 {'id':'C7','proposal':'Use translation of an arbitrary size-a seed subset in ZMod T to realize any sum when gcd(a,T)=1.','decision':'optional_interface_only','nearest_prior':['E102 translated support separation (different use)'],'delta':'No exact translated fixed-cardinality subset-sum interface found. It removes the interval shape from the existence mechanism.','limits':'Current ControllerIntervalSums already has a short interval-sum formula and explicit startFor. No immediate net shortening is established if interval APIs and exact witnesses are retained.'},
